  "title": "How to Use BIDMAS (Order of Operations)",
  "content": "<p><strong>BIDMAS</strong> tells you the order: <strong>B</strong>rackets, <strong>I</strong>ndices, <strong>D</strong>ivision and <strong>M</strong>ultiplication (left to right), <strong>A</strong>ddition and <strong>S</strong>ubtraction (left to right).</p><p>Division and multiplication share equal priority — work left to right. Same for addition and subtraction. The fraction bar acts like a bracket — evaluate top and bottom separately.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>Calculate</strong> \\(5 + 3 \\times 2^2 - (10 \\div 5)\\)</p><p><strong>Brackets:</strong> \\(10 \\div 5 = 2\\)</p><p><strong>Indices:</strong> \\(2^2 = 4\\)</p><p><strong>Multiplication:</strong> \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\)</p><p><strong>Left to right:</strong> \\(5 + 12 - 2 = 15\\)</p>"
 },
